<title>JAPAN: Tokyo corn market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo corn market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo corn futures market was closed on Monday for a holiday. The market reopens on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Prices were mostly lower on Friday as long-liquidation by local investors erased earlier price gains, traders said.</p>
<p>The spot November contract ended up 60 yen at 17,510 yen a tonne. Others were 60 to 250 yen lower, and the benchmark September contract was down 250 yen at 16,900.</p>
</text>
